        ("What is on an Excel test for a job?", "Most employer tests check formulas and references ($), lookups (VLOOKUP, XLOOKUP or INDEX/MATCH), SUMIFS and COUNTIFS, PivotTables, sorting and filtering, and often charts, conditional formatting and cleaning messy data. Many are done in a real workbook, so practise in Excel itself, not only by reading."),
        ("How can I test my Excel skills?", "Take a self-test like this one to see which areas you miss, then rebuild each answer in a real workbook. A good practical check: take a messy export, clean it, summarise it with a PivotTable and chart the result without looking anything up."),
        ("Is Excel hard to learn?", "The basics (typing data, SUM, sorting, filters) come quickly. Lookups, SUMIFS and PivotTables take more practice, and Power Query, dynamic arrays and macros more again. Most office jobs need the first two groups."),
