    ("When do filter and map in a Java stream actually run?", ["When a terminal operation such as toList or count is called", "As soon as filter is written", "When the program starts", "Only on a second thread"], 0, "Intermediate operations are lazy. They only describe the work, and the terminal operation pulls the data through."),
    ("What is Optional for?", ["Making a field private", "Running code in parallel", "Showing that a value may be missing, without returning null", "Declaring a method as not required"], 2, "It makes the empty case visible to the caller, who then uses methods such as orElse or ifPresent."),
